@@ -196,6 +196,24 @@ Rclone works fastest with large squashfs block sizes. For example:
 mksquashfs 100files 100files.sqfs -comp zstd -b 1M
 ```
 
+## Symbolic links
+
+Symbolic links stored in an archive are ignored unless `-l/--links`
+is in use. With `--links` each link is exposed as a regular file whose
+name has the `.rclonelink` suffix and whose contents are the link
+target, in the same way as the [local](/local/) backend. This means a
+link can be recreated on a destination which supports them:
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:s3:rclone/dir/100files.zip
+       12 2025-10-27 14:39:20.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2025-10-27 14:39:20.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:s3:rclone/dir/100files.zip /tmp/out
+```
+
+A regular file whose name happens to end in `.rclonelink` is still
+read as a regular file.
+
 ## Limitations
 
 Files in the archive backend are read only. It isn't possible to
